From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] spacemit: k1: don't require SPI NOR in SPL

The LicheePi 3A has no SPI NOR. Its SPL reached "DDR is ready" and then
nor_early_init() panicked with "Fail to detect spi controller" inside
board_init_f(), before board_boot_order() ever ran. This happens on a cold
boot too, so it isn't a stale boot flag. Log a missing SPI controller and
carry on to the eMMC/SD boot devices.
---
 board/spacemit/k1/spl.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/board/spacemit/k1/spl.c
+++ b/board/spacemit/k1/spl.c
@@ -419,9 +419,15 @@
 	struct udevice *dev;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Boards without SPI NOR (like the LicheePi 3A) still boot from eMMC
+	 * or SD, so don't stop here when there's no SPI controller.
+	 */
 	ret = uclass_get_device(UCLASS_SPI, 0, &dev);
-	if (ret)
-		panic("Fail to detect spi controller.\n");
+	if (ret) {
+		log_info("Fail to detect spi controller:%d\n", ret);
+		return;
+	}
 	udelay(10);
 	ret = uclass_get_device(UCLASS_SPI_FLASH, 0, &dev);
 	if (ret)
